From b2ee47b7f7efca3225974192284c1b418b201f31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Shaw <mshaw.cx@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:05:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mxl862xx: use the legacy PCS for SFP port 13 on old
 firmware

On firmware older than 1.0.84, mxl862xx_phylink_mac_select_pcs() returns
no PCS for any SerDes port, to leave the CPU port's SerDes in the mode
set in the switch's flash. Port 13 is caught by that too. On the BPI-R4
Pro it is the SFP cage (sfp-lan on the 4E, lan6 in SFP mode on the 8X),
and with no PCS phylink never sets its mode for the module or reads its
link state, so it stays down. The boards ship with firmware 1.0.70.

mxl862xx_setup_pcs() already gives every SerDes port the legacy PCS on
old firmware. It sets the mode with SYS_MISC_SFP_SET and reads link,
speed and duplex from the port. Return it for port 13 when that is a
user port, and keep no PCS for the others.

Tested on a BPI-R4 Pro 4E with firmware 1.0.70 and a 3 m passive DAC
(SFP-H10GB-CU3M): sfp-lan switches to 10gbase-r, links at 10Gbps/Full and
passes traffic, and the CPU port and lan1-4 come up as before. Other
modules and modes are untested.
---
 drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c b/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c
index 5cfc0a5..50dec75 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mxl862xx/mxl862xx-phylink.c
@@ -564,6 +564,14 @@ mxl862xx_phylink_mac_select_pcs(struct phylink_config *config,
 		if (READ_ONCE(priv->rescue_mode))
 			return NULL;
 		if (!MXL862XX_FW_VER_MIN(priv, 1, 0, 84)) {
+			/* Old firmware lacks the XPCS API, but the legacy PCS
+			 * can still set an SFP port's SerDes mode through
+			 * SYS_MISC_SFP_SET and read its link state. Without
+			 * a PCS the port never links. The CPU port's SerDes
+			 * stays in its flash-configured mode.
+			 */
+			if (port == 13 && dsa_port_is_user(dp))
+				return &priv->serdes_ports[port - 9].pcs;
 			dev_warn_once(dp->ds->dev,
 				      "SerDes PCS unsupported on old firmware.\n");
 			return NULL;
-- 
2.47.3

